    "dangerRationale": "Opens the recipe editor on an existing recipe for the user to review. It starts no terminals and saves nothing on its own.",
    "description": "Put a recipe draft in front of the user in the editor, either blank for a worktree or loaded from an existing recipe. This is a handoff, not a write: nothing is saved or deleted until the person reviews the draft and saves it, so a success here means the editor is open, never that the recipe exists. An unknown recipe opens a blank draft rather than failing.",
